# README Maintenance

`README.md` is the only top-level user-facing guide. Skill-internal
`SKILL.md` and reference files are allowed under `.cursor/skills/`.

## Audience & tone

- Write for **first-time users** who want cited research without learning the Valyu API
- Lead with outcomes and path choice; bury flag tables after a working example
- Conversational but concrete — short sentences, copy-pasteable commands
- Do **not** document `ship-it` (internal gate skill; not part of the research product)

## Style

- Title: `# VibeResearching ✨`
- Opening: bold tagline + one hook sentence (what you get, not how it works)
- Benefits / features: `**Name** — short em-dash explanation`
- Emoji sparingly (🚀 🧪 ⚡ 🎨 📚)
- Closing: friendly one-liner + emojis (e.g. **Happy researching!**)
- Prefer bullets, small tables, and bash/INI/JSON blocks over long prose

## Structure (required order)

1. Title + tagline
2. Why VibeResearching? 🚀
3. Pick a path — comprehensive / single-topic / multi-angle / enrich
   (+ optional verify) as a decision guide
4. Quick Start (≤3 commands: `pip`, `cp .env.example .env`)
5. First run — one concrete happy-path example (prefer deep or batch baseline)
6. Usage Examples — progressive (comprehensive → async single-topic →
   multi-angle retry → enrich → verify)
7. CLI Reference — one subsection per public runner below
8. Input/Output — `work/<topic-slug>/`, `work/deep/`, `work/batch/`, `work/enrich/` trees, ideas JSON, cost table
9. Configuration — `.env` table, priority, categories, sample INI (placeholders only)
10. License + sign-off

## CLI Reference sources of truth

Document argparse exactly — run `--help` or read `add_argument` in:

| README section | Script |
| --- | --- |
| `research-single-topic` | `.cursor/skills/research-single-topic/scripts/research_runner.py` |
| `research-multi-angle` | `.cursor/skills/research-multi-angle/scripts/research_runner.py` |
| `research-verify` | `.cursor/skills/research-verify/scripts/verify_references.py` |

- Include every command + flag (defaults, required, choices)
- `research-comprehensive` is an agent skill (no dedicated runner) — cover its
  chained fast → heavy → standard workflow using the single-topic and
  multi-angle runners with one `work/<topic-slug>/` directory
- `research-enrich` is an agent skill (no dedicated runner) — cover in
  Pick a path / Features; CLI examples reuse `research-multi-angle` with
  `work/enrich/` and `--max-queries 0`
- Skill workflow detail lives in `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` — README stays command-oriented
- Never document `ship-it` or removed skills (e.g. convert-pdf)

## Canonical paths

| Artifact | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Full reports | `work/<topic-slug>/research_init.md`, `work/<topic-slug>/research_deep.md`, `work/<topic-slug>/researchNN_*.md` |
| Full ideation / outcomes | `work/<topic-slug>/research_idea.md`, `work/<topic-slug>/ideas.json`, `work/<topic-slug>/manifest.json` |
| Deep reports | `work/deep/research_init.md`, `work/deep/research_deep.md` |
| Deep ideation | `work/deep/research_idea.md` |
| Batch reports | `work/batch/research_init.md`, `work/batch/researchNN_*.md` |
| Batch queries / outcomes | `work/batch/ideas.json`, `work/batch/manifest.json` |
| Temp state (all skills) | `{work dir}/tmp_state.json`, `tmp_checkpoint.json`, `tmp_checkpoint_response.json` — auto-removed on success |
| OpenAlex cache | `{report dir}/openalex_cache.json` (per directory; `--cache PATH` to share one) |
| Verify sidecars | `{report}.json` beside `{report}.md` (audit-only; never rewrite reports) |
| Enrich I/O | any user-supplied content (notes, drafts, articles, reports, outlines, presentations, any path/filename, `@` mention, or pasted text) → `work/enrich/` (`brief.md`, `ideas.json`, reports) |

Output examples must use these paths (`work/<topic-slug>/...`, `work/deep/...`, `work/batch/...`, `work/enrich/...`) — never invent alternate names. Do **not** prescribe input filenames for enrich; sources are whatever the user provides.

## Configuration rules

- Source of truth: `.env.example` (never paste real keys)
- Credentials: `VALYU_API_KEY` / `OPENALEX_API_KEY` > `[valyu]` /
  `[openalex]` INI
- Supported runtime settings: CLI flag > environment variable > INI
- Categories list must match `.env.example` comments
- Runtime research policy belongs in `valyu-api.mdc`, not this README rule

## Update when

- Any argparse option/default/subcommand changes in public research runners
- `requirements.txt` or `.env.example` changes
- New/renamed user-facing skill, workflow path, or artifact naming
- Mode cost estimates or `--max-cost` defaults change
- License or project display name changes

## Do / don't

- ✅ Decision guide before CLI encyclopedia
- ✅ Bullets, tables, and copy-pasteable commands
- ✅ Trees that list all generated artifacts
- ✅ Placeholder secrets only (`your-*-api-key-here`)
- ❌ Documenting `ship-it` (or any internal-only skill)
- ❌ Documenting removed skills / runners
- ❌ New top-level user guides besides README
- ❌ Documenting vibesliding `src.*.cli` modules (wrong repo)
- ❌ Stale flags, paths, or cost numbers after runner edits
